---
// terms.astro — Terms of Service (prerendered static).
// Modeled on gratisglobal.com's legal pages; adapted for a B2B data site
// with forward-looking account features and an attribution-based data
// reuse policy.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';

const updated = 'July 12, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that govern use of NSN Explorer, including accounts, acceptable use, data reuse with attribution, and disclaimers."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    These Terms of Service govern your use of the {SITE_NAME} website at nsnexplorer.com,
    including any account features as they become available (together, the "Services"). By using
    the Services, you agree to these terms.
  </p>
  <p class="mono updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <div class="note">
    <b>The short version.</b> {SITE_NAME} is a free reference that shows what the U.S. government
    paid for parts, built entirely from public official records, with a link to the source behind
    every figure. Use it lawfully, don't hammer our servers, and feel free to reuse the data with
    attribution. We sell nothing here and recommend nothing; the records speak for themselves.
  </div>

  <h2>1. What {SITE_NAME} is</h2>
  <p>
    The Services are a compiled, searchable presentation of public U.S. government procurement
    records — award notices, contract actions, and related logistics data published by government
    sources such as DIBBS and USAspending.gov. We organize those records by National Stock Number
    and link every figure we display to the official record it came from. We do not create,
    estimate, or model prices, and we do not control the underlying government sources, whose
    content and availability can change at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Eligibility and business use</h2>
  <p>
    The Services are intended for professional and business use. You must be old enough to form a
    binding contract in your jurisdiction. If you use the Services on behalf of a company or other
    organization, you represent that you are authorized to accept these terms for it, and "you"
    includes that organization.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Accounts</h2>
  <p>
    Some features may require an account as they launch, such as saved searches, watchlists, or
    alerts. When account features are available, you agree to provide accurate information, keep
    your credentials secure, and take responsibility for activity under your account. You may
    delete your account at any time. We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these terms
    or that we reasonably believe pose a risk to the Services or other users.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>When using the Services, you agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the Services for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable law or third-party rights.</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Services, other users' accounts, or our systems.</li>
    <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Services, including by introducing malware or overloading our infrastructure.</li>
    <li>Crawl or bulk-download the Services with automated tools in a way that burdens our systems or circumvents technical limits. If you want the data at volume, email us — there is probably an easier way for both of us.</li>
    <li>Misrepresent your identity or affiliation, or present {SITE_NAME} data in a way that misattributes it to us after altering it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Data reuse and attribution</h2>
  <p>
    The procurement records we present are public information published by the U.S. government,
    and we believe they should stay usable. You may reuse, quote, and republish the data we
    display — including prices, dates, and source links — for any lawful purpose, commercial or
    not, provided you attribute {SITE_NAME} with a link to the relevant page (or to
    {SITE_URL}) where practical. This permission covers the data itself; it does not cover our
    branding or original writing (see <a href="#ip">Intellectual property</a>), and it does not
    replace the terms of the underlying government sources, which remain the authoritative
    records.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Accuracy; no advice</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to present records faithfully — our build refuses to publish a price without its
    source link — but official records can contain errors, can lag actual events, and can be
    revised by the government after we ingest them. The Services are provided for reference and
    research. Nothing on the Services is procurement, pricing, legal, or investment advice, and no
    figure here should be treated as a quote or an offer. Always verify against the linked source
    record before relying on a figure.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Third-party sites and records</h2>
  <p>
    The Services link out to records and websites operated by third parties, including U.S.
    government systems. We do not control those sites, and we are not responsible for their
    content, accuracy, availability, or practices. Your use of third-party sites is governed by
    their own terms and policies. If something you reach through the Services appears wrong or
    unlawful, please tell us using the contact details below.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The Services may include advertising, which helps keep them free. Advertising is subject to
    our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. Advertisements and any offers within them are the
    responsibility of the advertiser, and we are not responsible for third-party products or
    services promoted through advertising.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ip">9. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The {SITE_NAME} name, logo, site design, original text, and software are owned by
    {SITE_NAME} and protected by intellectual property laws. Apart from the data reuse permission
    in section 5, you may not copy, reproduce, or reuse our branding or original materials without
    permission. The underlying government records are public information and remain subject to
    the policies of the agencies that publish them.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you believe content on the Services infringes your rights, contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with enough detail to identify the
    material in question, and we will respond appropriately.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    The Services are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, whether
    express or implied, including any warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
    purpose, and non-infringement. We do not warrant that the Services will be uninterrupted,
    error-free, or secure, or that any record displayed is complete, current, or free of errors
    introduced by its government source.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} and its operators will not be liable for
    any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of profits,
    data, use, or goodwill, arising out of or related to your use of the Services or any decision
    made in reliance on data displayed by them. To the fullest extent permitted by law, our total
    liability for any claim relating to the Services will not exceed one hundred US dollars.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Indemnification</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {SITE_NAME} and its operators from any claims,
    damages, and expenses, including reasonable legal fees, arising from your misuse of the
    Services or violation of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to the Services and these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may change, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Services at any time. We may also
    update these terms from time to time. When we make material changes, we will update the date
    at the top of this page. Your continued use of the Services after an update means you accept
    the revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} is operated by a Wyoming limited liability company. These terms are governed by
    the laws of the United States and the State of Wyoming, without regard to conflict-of-law
    principles. Any disputes will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and
    federal courts located in Wyoming, unless applicable law requires otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? Email us at
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
